<title>USA: Digital Biometrics chairman stepping down.</title>
<headline>Digital Biometrics chairman stepping down.</headline>
<dateline>MINNETONKA, Minn. 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digital Biometrics Inc said Jack Klingert, 67, was retiring as chairman and would also give up the chief executive post once a successor was found.</p>
<p>The manufacturer of identification and security products said it named C. McKenzie Lewis, a board member since 1993, as chairman to provide continuity during the transition.</p>
</text>
